@startuml CL12_ReviewTool
!include _style.iuml
title CL-12  Review tool — step through review.xlsx and adjust the working circle (Python 3, Tkinter; Pillow, openpyxl; macOS and Windows)

package "allsky_review  (tools/review)" {
  class ReviewApp {
    -session : ReviewSession
    -frame : FrameView
    -metrics : MetricsPanel
    -table : ReviewTable
    +run(run_folder)
    -restore_state() / save_state()
      .review-state.json in the run folder:
      last row and filter
    keys: C Clear · X Cloud · U Unsure ·
      ↑ ↓ or mouse wheel previous / next ·
      N next unreviewed · Delete clears my verdict ·
      F filter · S working circle
    -preview : WorkingArea?
    .. REQ-62 REQ-63 ..
  }
  class ReviewSession {
    -rows : list[ReviewRow]
    -filter : RowFilter
    -index : int
    +current : ReviewRow
    +shown_rows() : list[ReviewRow]
    +next() / previous() / next_unreviewed()
    +go_to(row) : bool
    +restore(excel_row, filter_name)
    +record(verdict)  saves, then moves on
    +set_filter(filter)
    +tally() : Tally
    .. REQ-62 ..
  }
  class ReviewWorkbook {
    +load(run_folder) : list[ReviewRow]
    +set_verdict(row, verdict)
    +save()
    +is_open_in_excel() : bool
    +settings_path() : Path?
    +run_working_area() : WorkingArea?
    +original_image(row) : Path?
    from the Settings sheet the harness wrote
    .. REQ-61 REQ-62 REQ-63 ..
  }
  class ReviewRow <<dataclass>> {
    +excel_row : int
    +night, local_time, target : str
    +verdict : Clear | Cloud | Unknown
    +stars_found, stars_expected : int
    +star_fraction, brightness, uniformity : float?
    +picked_because : str
    +image : Path
    +my_verdict : Clear | Cloud | Unsure | None
    +agrees : bool?
    .. REQ-62 ..
  }
  enum RowFilter {
    ALL
    UNREVIEWED
    MONITOR_CLOUD
    MONITOR_CLEAR
    DISAGREE
    .. REQ-62 ..
  }
  class Tally <<dataclass>> {
    +total, reviewed, agree, disagree : int
    +false_cloud, missed_cloud : int
    +agreement : float?
    .. REQ-62 ..
  }
  class FrameView {
    +show(image : Path)
    +show_image(image, message)
    +zoom_at(x, y)  click: 1× → 3× → fit
    .. REQ-62 ..
  }
  class ReviewTable {
    +show(rows, current)
    one line per row in the filter: Excel row,
    night, time, target, both verdicts, Agrees,
    metrics, why; disagreements in red;
    picking a line calls on_pick(row)
    .. REQ-62 ..
  }
  class MetricsPanel {
    +show(row : ReviewRow, position, tally : Tally)
    .. REQ-62 ..
  }
  class WorkbookOpenError <<exception>>
  class WorkingArea <<dataclass>> {
    +centre_alt, centre_az, radius : float
    +validate()
    .. REQ-63 ..
  }
  class LensModel {
    +to_pixel(alt, az) : (x, y)
    port of LensProjection.ToPixel
    .. REQ-63 ..
  }
  class WorkingCircleDrawing <<module>> {
    +destination(alt, az, bearing, distance)
    +circle_pixels(lens, area)
    +draw_working_area(frame, lens, area, outline, title) : Image
    port of SkyGeometry.Destination and the
    harness's drawing (AnnotatedFrameWriter)
    .. REQ-63 ..
  }
  class SettingsFile {
    +path : Path
    +lens, outline, working_area
    +save_working_area(area)
    .. REQ-63 ..
  }
  class SettingsWindow <<Toplevel>> {
    centre altitude, azimuth, radius
    "run used: alt / az / radius"
    Apply · Save · Revert · Close
    .. REQ-63 ..
  }
  class "requirement()" as Req <<decorator>> {
    tags classes and tests with REQ ids,
    like [Requirement] in C#
  }
}

ReviewApp --> ReviewSession
ReviewApp --> FrameView
ReviewApp --> MetricsPanel
ReviewApp --> ReviewTable
ReviewApp --> SettingsWindow
ReviewApp ..> WorkingCircleDrawing
SettingsWindow --> SettingsFile
SettingsFile ..> WorkingArea
WorkingCircleDrawing ..> LensModel
WorkingCircleDrawing ..> WorkingArea
ReviewSession --> ReviewWorkbook
ReviewSession o-- "*" ReviewRow
ReviewSession ..> RowFilter
ReviewSession ..> Tally
ReviewWorkbook ..> ReviewRow
ReviewWorkbook ..> WorkbookOpenError

note bottom of ReviewWorkbook
  Reads the Review sheet of review.xlsx written by the harness
  (CL-11a), finding columns by their headings; the image path comes
  from the HYPERLINK formula. Writes only the My verdict column, so the
  drop-down, the Agrees formulas and the Summary sheet stay intact
  (Excel recalculates them when opened). Saved after every verdict,
  to a temporary file then renamed. Excel's lock file (~$review.xlsx)
  means the workbook is open: the save is refused with a message and
  retried on the next verdict, nothing is lost.
  Asks Excel to recalculate on opening, since
  openpyxl keeps no cached formula results.
end note
note bottom of SettingsFile
  The settings.json given to the harness (path from the
  Settings sheet, or chosen). Writes back only CentreAltDeg,
  CentreAzDeg, RadiusDeg (and the informational Centre copy);
  every other value is kept as read. The first save keeps the
  file as settings.json.bak; saves go to a temporary file then
  rename. The plugin's own settings on the AstroPC are not
  touched: the imager enters the three values there.
end note
note bottom of LensModel
  Same maths as Core: r = c1·z + c2·z² + … (z = zenith distance),
  angle = north rotation ± azimuth. No altitude clamp, so a circle
  below the horizon is drawn as the harness draws it. A shared
  table of alt/az → pixel cases is checked by both the C# and the
  Python tests.
end note
note bottom of ReviewSession
  Starts at the first row without a verdict, or
  where the last session stopped (restore).
  Filters: all, not reviewed, monitor said Cloud,
  monitor said Clear, verdicts disagree.
  Tally matches the Summary sheet.
end note
@enduml
